1
00:00:00,530 --> 00:00:06,770
I am so grateful to be here with all of you as we discuss the Artemis program and announce

2
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:11,210
the four astronauts who will undertake this very exciting mission.

3
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:21,170
Making his first space flight, mission specialist Andre Douglas, record-setting astronaut, mission

4
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:26,790
specialist Colonel Frank Riviere.

5
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:34,430
Now onto our pilot, East astronaut Luca Carmatano.

6
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:42,840
Now to our Commander, Marine Corps Colonel Artemis III Commander, Randy Bresley.

7
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:49,180
Artemis III backup crew member, Bob Hines.

8
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:56,700
One more round of applause for your Artemis III Prime Crew.

9
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:02,540
We are certainly humbled as a crew to be able to be your crew that executes this Artemis

10
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:04,380
III mission in space.

11
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:08,580
Being that unifying link between the phenomenal Artemis II mission we just had two months

12
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:12,980
ago and the Artemis IV mission that will follow ours.

13
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:20,740
While Artemis II was all about moon joy, Artemis III will be all about Earth joy.

14
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:27,260
We will study Earth's atmosphere, the environment around Orion during the mission and the impact

15
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:31,260
of space's influence within the Orion capsule.

16
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:36,420
Artemis III is an incredibly exciting, complicated, and highly coordinated multi-launch campaign.

17
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:39,780
It's going to happen in a short period of time with three of the world's most

18
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:40,780
powerful rockets.

19
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:44,860
So to the Artemis III crew, we wish you God's speed on the journey ahead.

20
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:50,140
You carry the fire of exploration from generations past, the confidence of this agency, and

21
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,660
the support of this nation.

22
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:55,300
The Artemis II crew, comrade, hands you the baton.

23
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,140
You got the controls.

